The theming system is built on **tokenized CSS variables**: every panel color derives from a set of tokens; presets and custom overrides are deep-merged and injected into `:root` (or a target container).

## Presets

| Preset | Primary | Hover |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `nyx` (default) | `rgb(10, 116, 38)` | `rgb(10, 116, 38)` |
| `shokax` | `rgb(233, 84, 107)` | `#ed6ea0` |

```tsx
<NyxPlayer urls={urls} preset="shokax" />
```

## Custom token overrides

`styles` deep-merges `light` / `dark` token groups (returns a **new object**, never mutates presets):

```tsx
<NyxPlayer
  urls={urls}
  styles={{
    styles: {
      light: { primary: "rgb(80, 140, 220)", hoverBtn: "#2d6cdf" },
      dark: { primary: "rgb(120, 180, 255)", hoverBtn: "#5ea2ff" },
    },
  }}
/>
```

### All tokens

| Token | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `background` | Panel background |
| `border` | Panel border |
| `closeBtn` | Close button color |
| `primaryText` / `secondaryText` | Primary / secondary text |
| `playlistLine` | Playlist divider |
| `hoverBtn` | Hover accent |
| `shadow` | Panel shadow |
| `primary` / `primaryRgb` | Primary color (`rgb(...)`) and its RGB components |

```ts
interface ThemeTokens {
  background: string;
  border: string;
  closeBtn: string;
  primaryText: string;
  secondaryText: string;
  playlistLine: string;
  hoverBtn: string;
  shadow: string;
  primary: string;
  primaryRgb: string;
}
```

## Dark mode

| Value | Behavior |
| --- | --- |
| `"auto"` | Follows system `prefers-color-scheme` |
| CSS selector (e.g. `html[data-theme='dark']`) | Target exists = dark; `MutationObserver` tracks attribute changes in real time |

```tsx
// follow the system
<NyxPlayer urls={urls} darkModeTarget="auto" />

// follow a blog's data-theme attribute
<NyxPlayer urls={urls} darkModeTarget="html[data-theme='dark']" />
```

## Programmatic theming

```ts
import { presets, resolveTheme, applyThemeTokens, useTheme } from "nyx-player-solid";

// resolve (deep-merged, new object)
const theme = resolveTheme({ preset: "shokax", custom: styles });

// apply to a container
applyThemeTokens(document.documentElement, theme.styles.light);

// Solid hook: follows the dark-mode signal and injects CSS variables
useTheme({ preset, custom, darkModeTarget });
```

The core layer is framework-agnostic (no `solid-js` / DOM dependency) and available from the top-level `nyx-player-solid` entry.

## PlayerCore

The playback state machine (unidirectional: action → setState → notify; audio side effects are internal — no event bus).

```ts
const core = new PlayerCore({ adapter?, provider?, initialMode?, initialVolume? });
await core.init(sources);
core.play(); core.pause(); core.toggle();
core.next(); core.prev();
core.seek(30); core.setMode("random"); core.cycleMode();
core.setVolume(0.5); core.toggleMute();
core.selectPlaylist(1); core.playSong(1, 2);
core.back(); core.forward(); core.clearHistory();
const state = core.getState();
const unsubscribe = core.subscribe((next) => ...);
```

### PlayerState fields

`playing` / `currentTime` / `duration` / `mode`(`order|random|loop`) / `playlists` / `playlistNames` / `playlistIndex` / `perSongIndex` / `perLastIndex` / `volume` / `muted` / `loading` / `error`.

### Current track

```ts
import { currentSongOf } from "nyx-player-solid";
const song = currentSongOf(core.getState()); // Song | null
```

### Play history

`getHistory(): HistoryEntry[]`, `HistoryEntry = { playlistIndex, songIndex }`. `back`/`forward` are browser-style navigation; explicit navigation (next/prev/playSong) drops the forward branch.

## AudioAdapter

`AudioAdapter` is the only layer allowed to touch the real audio engine (default `HTMLAudioAdapter`; injectable for tests/custom).

```ts
interface AudioAdapter {
  setSrc(url: string): void;
  play(): Promise<void>;            // may be rejected by autoplay policy
  pause(): void;
  seek(time: number): void;
  setVolume(v: number): void;
  setMuted(m: boolean): void;
  getCurrentTime(): number;
  getDuration(): number;
  on(event: AudioAdapterEvent, handler: () => void): () => void;
  getContextAnalysis?(): AnalyserNode | null; // R4: visualization
  dispose(): void;
}
```

Events: `timeupdate` / `ended` / `error` / `loadedmetadata` / `play` / `pause`.

## Lyrics parsing

| Function | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `parseLyric(text)` | Standard LRC → `LyricLine[]` (`{ text, start, end }`, end auto-aligned) |
| `parseLyricLine(line)` | Single-line timestamp → seconds (throws on invalid) |
| `findActiveLyricIndex(lines, time)` | Locate the active line (linear, falls back to the last line) |
| `parseWordLyric(text)` | LLRC word timestamps → `WordLyricLine[]` (degrades to whole-line for plain LRC, **LRC-compatible**) |
| `activeWordIndex(words, time)` | Karaoke: last active word index |
| `fetchLyricText(urlOrText)` | Fetch by URL / return inline text directly (bounded cache, 8s timeout) |

## Other utilities

- `runWithPool(items, limit, fn)` / `ConcurrencyPool`: concurrency-limited execution (playlist fetching)
- `parsePlaylistUrl(url)` / `hasPlaylistURL(url)`: playlist URL resolution (netease / tencent)
- `createHTMLAudioAdapter(element?)`: browser audio adapter (accepts an existing `<audio>` element)
- `createNoopAdapter()`: SSR-safe no-op

`MetadataProvider` resolves a `PlaylistSource` into playable `Song[]`. Three built-in providers:

```ts
interface MetadataProvider {
  readonly name: string;
  match(source: PlaylistSource): boolean;
  fetchSongs(source: PlaylistSource): Promise<Song[]>;
}
```

## directProvider

```ts
import { directProvider } from "nyx-player-solid";

// singleton: consumes source.songs directly, no network
```

## createMetingProvider (music sources)

Resolves playlist URLs (Netease / QQ Music etc.) through the meting API:

```ts
import { createMetingProvider } from "nyx-player-solid";

const provider = createMetingProvider({
  baseURL: "https://api.injahow.cn/meting/", // self-hosted endpoints welcome
  timeoutMs: 10_000,
  maxRetries: 3,
});
```

| Option | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `baseURL` | `https://api.injahow.cn/meting/` | meting API endpoint; self-hosted supported (e.g. `https://your-host/meting/`) |
| `timeoutMs` | `10_000` | Per-request timeout |
| `maxRetries` | `3` | Max retries (exponential backoff) |
| `fetchImpl` | `globalThis.fetch` | fetch implementation (test injection) |

## createCompositeProvider

Combines providers in `match` order; one failure doesn't block the rest:

```ts
import { createCompositeProvider, directProvider, createMetingProvider } from "nyx-player-solid";

const provider = createCompositeProvider([directProvider, createMetingProvider()]);
// <NyxPlayer provider={provider} urls={...} />
```

`<NyxPlayer>` defaults to this combination.

## URL parsing

```ts
import { parsePlaylistUrl, hasPlaylistURL } from "nyx-player-solid";

const result = parsePlaylistUrl("https://music.163.com/#/playlist?id=123");
// { id: "123", provider: "netease", type: "playlist" }
// type: "song" | "album" | "artist" | "playlist"
```

- Supports Netease `music.163.com` and QQ Music `y.qq.com` / `i.y.qq.com`
- `hasPlaylistURL(source)`: whether `source.url` is a recognizable playlist URL

## Custom providers

```ts
import type { MetadataProvider } from "nyx-player-solid";

const myProvider: MetadataProvider = {
  name: "my-source",
  match: (source) => source.url?.startsWith("https://my-music.example/") ?? false,
  async fetchSongs(source) {
    const res = await fetch(source.url!);
    const json = await res.json();
    return json.songs.map(/* → Song[] */);
  },
};

<NyxPlayer urls={urls} provider={myProvider} />;
```

